{"name":"Puffins Bill","hex":"#e95c20","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"puffins","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of puffin"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puffins"},{"term":"bill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A written list or inventory. (Now obsolete except in specific senses or set phrases; bill of lading, bill of goods, etc.)","A document, originally sealed; a formal statement or official memorandum. (Now obsolete except with certain qualifying words; bill of health, bill of sale etc.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To advertise by a bill or public notice.","To charge; to send a bill to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Puffin","blocks":[{"text":"Puffins are any of three species of small alcids (auks) in the bird genus Fratercula. These are pelagic seabirds that feed primarily by diving in the water. They breed in large colonies on coastal cliffs or offshore islands, nesting in crevices among rocks or in burrows in the soil. Two species, the tufted puffin and horned puffin, are found in the North Pacific Ocean, while the Atlantic puffin is found in the North Atlantic Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Papageitaucher_Fratercula_arctica.jpg/330px-Papageitaucher_Fratercula_arctica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puffin","wikidata":"Q311761"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Wiki-utou2.jpg/500px-Wiki-utou2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Wiki-utou2.jpg/1280px-Wiki-utou2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Wiki-utou2.jpg/500px-Wiki-utou2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm